  "description": "Change of use from Use Class C3 (dwelling house) to Use Class C4 (HMO-house in multiple occupation), involving  removal of chimney and changes to side/rear fenestration's with associated amenity, cycle and refuse storage.\r",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice. \rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby approved shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans with the approved plans which forms part of this notice. \r \rLocation Plan; Highway Impact Assessment; Planning statement; Fire Strategy; 301; 202; 100.\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning. \r",
    "No independent cooking or laundry facilities shall be installed in any of the respective bedrooms, and the communal kitchen and dining room (ground floor) and shall be retained as such, in accordance with the approved plans, in perpetuity.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied until the cycle parking spaces proposed have been fully constructed in accordance with the hereby approved details and shall thereafter be retained for the lifetime of the development.  \r\rReason: To ensure that adequate cycle parking facilities are provided to promote sustainable modes of transport. \r",
    "The refuse and recycling storage hereby approved shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details and thereafter maintained unless otherwise in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\r\rReason: In the interests of amenity and the recycling of waste materials in support of the Boroughs waste reduction targets. \r",
    "The use of the property as a House in Multiple Occupation hereby approved shall be occupied by a maximum of 6 people at any one time and shall not be subdivided or occupied as self-contained units. \r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "The new ground floor side facing window serving the WC shall be fixed shut and in obscured glass with an equivalent obscuration as level 3 on the Pilkington Obscuration Range unless 1.7m above the floor level of the room to which it relates. The glazing shall not be altered without the approval in writing of the Local Planning Authority. \r\rReason: To safeguard the privacy of the occupiers of adjoining and neighbouring properties.\r"
  ],
